   879	i.e. both terms are divisible by $q$. Then $q$ also divides
   880	\[ (a_1 a_2 + c_1 c_2) + (a_1 a_2 - c_1 a_2) = 2 a_1 a_{2 .} \]
   881	Since $q \neq 2, 3$, neither $a_1$nor $a_2$ is divisible by $q$, and so this
   882	is impossible. The same argument proves the second statement. \ $\Box$
