   892	a_2$.
   893	
   894	{\tmstrong{Proof}} \ a) If $q$ divides $c_2 - c_1 a_2$, then
   895	\[ a_1 = \frac{a_1}{a_2} a_2 \tmop{and} c_1 = \frac{a_1}{a_2} c_2
   896	   \tmop{modulo} q . \]
   897	Hence
   898	\[ 0 = m b_1 = a_1^2 + c_1^2 = \frac{a_1}{a_2} ( \text{$a_1 a_2 + c_1 c_2$})
   899	   \tmop{modulo} q, \]
   900	which in turn implies
