   976	c_1 a_2$, which \ is non-zero by our assumption . This implies $m^2 < a_1 c_2$
   977	or $m^2 < c_1 a_2$. In either case, $m$ is smaller than at least one of the
   978	four numbers $a_1$, $c_1$, $a_2$, $c_2$, which is impossible. If $m$ is even,
   979	then $a_1$, $c_1$, $a_2$, $c_2$ are odd, and so $a_1 c_2 - c_1 a_2$ is even.
   980	It follows that $\frac{m^2}{2}$ divides $a_1 c_2 - c_1 a_2$. As in the
   981	reasoning above we infer that $\frac{m}{\sqrt[]{2}}$ is less than at least one
   982	of the four numbers $a_1$, $c_1$, $a_2$, $c_2$, which is impossible since the
   983	dominant member of a Markoff triple exceeds the others by at least a factor 6.
