-"""Verified generator from arXiv:0709.1499, Section 2.
+"""Verified generator from arXiv:0709.1499, Propositions 2.1 and 2.2.
 
-The paper writes down the (up to scale) infinitesimal automorphism R of the
-upper-unitriangular matrix M(a,b,c).  It explicitly allows a,b,c to lie in an
-arbitrary commutative ring.  This generator substitutes sparse polynomials in
-Z[x] for a,b,c and asks for the normalized polynomial matrix R(x).
+The paper gives the infinitesimal automorphism R of an upper-unitriangular
+bilinear-form matrix M(a,b,c), over any commutative ring, and proves that the
+generator is carried through an integral change of basis by conjugation.  This
+module substitutes monomials in Z[x], hides M behind a unimodular basis, and
+asks for the correspondingly conjugated polynomial generator.
 
-Generation composes the displayed polynomial identity with a substitution; it
-never solves the generated coefficient-matching system.
+Generation composes displayed identities and a structure-preserving change of
