+commutative ring, displays a nonzero matrix `R` satisfying
+`R^T M + M R = 0`, and gives the change-of-basis law in Proposition 2.1(b).
 
-`M(a,b,c) = [[1,a,b],[0,1,c],[0,0,1]]`
