codex
Completed a verified native algebra generator on `TRACK = "B"`.

It uses the paper’s Section 2 matrix identity and Proposition 2.1 change-of-basis law, not its withdrawn headline theorem. The [arXiv record confirms the withdrawal](https://arxiv.org/abs/0709.1499).

Key results:

- All G1–G9 gates pass.
- Structured guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four attacks: each 0/8.
- Reference solver: 1,047,704 operations, 0.060 seconds.
- Bare oracle loop: 0/3 solved; verdict `hardened`.
- Shipping preset: `easy`, \(n=60\).
- Worst sampled answer: 1,300 characters, 210 atoms, approximately 325 tokens.
- G9 structural/placebo arms: both 1/3, giving a measured effect of 0.0.

Deliverables:

- [gen_0709_1499.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0709.1499/gen_0709_1499.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0709.1499/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0709.1499/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0709.1499/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0709.1499/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0709.1499/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)
- [.meta.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0709.1499/.meta.json)

The README records the important caveat that the installed harness used two vendors across three calls, rather than the four-vendor pool described in the task.
